keywords:
  - agent-based simulation
  - anthropology
  - archaeology
  - reproducibility
  - demography
  - migration
  - temporary mobility
  - aggregation
abstract: >-
  AnthroSim is a reproducible agent-based simulation framework for deterministic
  demography, resource-constrained permanent household migration,
  evidence-grounded spatial experiments, and explicit temporary mobility and
  aggregation under declared model assumptions. Version 0.3.0 is the audited M9
  release baseline. It adds persistent-residence versus physical-presence
  semantics, deterministic multi-day temporary journeys, duration-aware resource
  attribution, temporary-presence observability, and a controlled aggregation
  capability benchmark while preserving the M8 evidence-grounded spatial path.
  AnthroSim is not an empirically validated model of human prehistory.
